[[2047,96,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The supply for the centre module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               arrives\ndirectly from the battery. (maxifuse J/B1 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) to pin\n2 via fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; the supply controlled\nby the ignition (INT) reaches pin 1 of the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 3 is earthed.</p><p>The standard engine temperature sender unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends\na signal proportional to the temperature of the engine coolant to\npin 10 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . The minimum temperature signal, on the other\nhand, arrives at pin 9 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from the engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\ndepending on the different engine types.</p><p>This signal is sent again from pin 12 to\nthe Infocenter module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234378\">E4024</a></p><p>Pins 4 and 5 of the centre instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive\nsignals (positive and negative) coming from the fuel gauge \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               located\nin the fuel pump assembly. These signals pass through the speedometer\nmodule \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The signal for the warning lights test reaches\npin 6 and the lighting signal, also coming from the speedometer\nmodule \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , reaches pin 7.</p><p>Pin 11 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends a &#x27;fuel reserve&#x27;\nsignal to the engine management control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong><a href=\"#/3234515\">E5030</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"]]